  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nA touch-probe tool type and a **Probe** operation that finds a face, an edge, an outside corner, or a bore/boss centre, then sets a work offset (G54-G59) or stops for the operator. A found position outside the tolerance stops the program with a message.\r\n\r\n- **Tool:** `ToolKind::Probe` - `diameter` is the stylus ball, `flute_len` the stylus length, corner = ball radius. The starter catalog gains `PRB-0400` (4 mm ball, 30 mm stylus).\r\n- **Operation:** modes face (+-X/+-Y/-Z), edge, outside corner (two touches), bore centre and boss centre (four touches each). Every parameter has a default: approach clearance, probe distance (overtravel), back-off, seek and measure feeds, depth, corner inset, tolerance, result action. Created and edited through `CreateOperation` / `EditOperationParams`, so edits undo.\r\n- **Stable ids:** Probe is appended as kind id 38, so no existing op type id, digest tag or ribbon pin moves. The project format stays v50 and old projects load with no op going Stale. The menu lists Probe in the Drilling section by display order; the ribbon laws now ask for table order within a section instead of a contiguous run.\r\n- **Motion:** each touch is a fast seek, a back-off and a slow measuring re-probe, after an opening positioning rapid. The moves stay the nominal truth; `Toolpath::probes` (`cl::ProbeTouch`) marks which feeds are probing moves, their probe target and the measurement number. The project file saves them, so a reloaded op can never post a probe move as a plain feed.\r\n- **Post:** neutral stream records `TOUCH` / `RETREAT` / `FOUND` and hooks `onProbeMove` / `onProbeRetreat` / `onProbeResult`, with no prelude default.\r\n  - `fanuc.cps` writes G31 skip blocks with custom macro B. The trip is read from `#5061`-`#5063` and kept in `#100+3k`.\r\n  - Each skip block is followed by a no-contact alarm (`#3000=2`).\r\n  - The back-off is incremental (G91), so a part nearer than the model is never driven into.\r\n  - Then the tolerance stop (`#3000=1`), and `G10 L2 Pn` from `#5221 + 20 x slot`, or `#3006=1` to stop for the operator.\r\n  - A probe section starts no spindle and no coolant.\r\n  - Every other post refuses the op by name (`probing: operation \"Probe1\": this post script does not define onProbeMove ...`).\r\n- **Verify/sim:** probe moves are protected moves. The stylus ball is swept along every move against the model, and coming nearer than its radius anywhere is a `Gouge`, which holds the post. Probe ops skip the cutting and turning laws and remove no stock in the sim or the rest masks.\r\n- **UI:** the op appears in the operation menu with an original icon (`assets/ui/probe.png`, recorded in `LICENSES.md`) and a parameter page.\r\n- Decisions are recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` under \"#108 - Probe\".\r\n\r\n## Caveat: G31 on a real control\r\n\r\nThe G31 / custom macro B output is unverified on a real control. The skip-position variables (`#5061`-`#5063`), the work-offset variables (`#5221 + 20 x slot`) and the `#3000` / `#3006` stops come from Fanuc's public operator documentation as I understand it; no controller or simulator has run this code. **Check the control's manual before running it on a machine.** The golden locks the text, not the machine behaviour.\r\n\r\n## Pins (`crates/app/tests/probe_op.rs`, 10 tests)\r\n\r\n- `each_mode_lays_down_its_touches` - generation for all five modes, with the expected touches.\r\n- `bore_centre_posts_g31_skips_on_the_generic_dialect` - golden `tests/golden/nc/fanuc/probe_bore_centre.nc`; also checks the stream round-trips.\r\n- `a_dialect_without_probing_refuses_the_op_by_name` - the Heidenhain refusal.\r\n- `the_probe_round_trips_through_the_project_file`\r\n- `a_probe_param_edit_undoes_and_redoes`\r\n- `a_stylus_driven_through_material_is_a_gouge`\r\n- `a_face_touch_on_the_stock_top_generates_clean_and_cuts_nothing`\r\n- `degenerate_probe_numbers_are_refused`\r\n- `the_probe_row_appends_and_lists_in_drilling`\r\n- `every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag`\r\n\r\nAlso `ribbon::the_probe_appends_its_id_and_lists_in_drilling`.\r\n\r\n## Readings (after merging origin/main)\r\n\r\n| Suite | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| camcraft-app lib (incl. registry and `turning_rapids` tests) | 74 passed |\r\n| probe_op | 10 passed |\r\n| ribbon | 11 passed |\r\n| project_roundtrip | 68 passed |\r\n| conformance | 6 passed |\r\n| posting | 17 passed |\r\n| operations | 117 passed, 6 ignored (heavy lane) |\r\n| vertical_rapid_stock | 4 passed |\r\n| camcraft-sim vertical_rapids | 16 passed |\r\n| camcraft-post post_engine / comp | 30 / 6 passed |\r\n\r\nClippy `-D warnings`, all targets, on tools / cl / motion / sim / post / app / ui: clean. Before the merge, all camcraft-app test binaries except the slow `center_cut_multiaxis` passed, as did cl, tools, the motion lib and `one_descent`, and the sim lib and touched tests. UI test binaries compile but were not run, because they open the GUI.\r\n\r\n## Owed\r\n\r\n- #171 - create the op from a picked face, edge, vertex or cylinder (the contact point is typed today)\r\n- #172 - include the stylus shank and probe body in the collision check\r\n- #173 - probing hooks for the Haas, Mazak, Siemens and Heidenhain posts\r\n- #174 - a stop-on-contact (G38.3-style) protected descent before each touch\r\n\r\nChangelog: Probe operation: face, edge, outside-corner and bore/boss-centre finding with a touch probe - G31 skip touches on the Fanuc post with a no-contact alarm, set G54-G59 or stop for the operator, out-of-tolerance stop; posts that cannot probe refuse it by name (#108)\r\n\r\nRefs #108\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
